## What is 'cool'?
Let's first define what I mean with *cool* in the following. For that we need to establish a baseline. Of course, I didn't select the cards *fully randomly*. I hid specific strategic items like *Vranistan*, an imaginary country noone *can* have an opinion about. We see that (like expected), it fully mirrors the natural bias people had.

<DataFrame path="ranking-everything-baselines.csv" {...baseline} />

Let's define *cool* items to be above this baseline of $\approx67\%$ and *(un)coolness* the probability that the items are above/below this baseline due to systematic opinion, not coincidence (see appendix [1](#baseline), [2](#t-test) ).

