## Limitations

<div class="todo">

Working title. **Suggested** section: a short list here, so the rest of the post doesn't have to hedge.

- The crowd: ~44 devices from friends, the Uni Würzburg Discord and Instagram, nearly all DE. "What this crowd thinks", not "what people think"
- ~30 votes per item: wide intervals, most item-level results are descriptive
- Votes are not independent (one device judges many items); the per-item binomial test assumes they are. The Rasch model in A model of taste is the fix
- Forking paths: battles and pairs picked after seeing the data. Separate the ones fixed in advance (the research items) from the ones found later
- A photo stands in for a concept (Florbish)

</div>

